WEBVTT

00:02.940 --> 00:06.130
If you can avoid drinking 
it, I'd prefer you don't.

00:07.100 --> 00:11.890
I wouldn't mind you being an undead forever.

00:12.980 --> 00:17.800
Just stay here forever and spend 
your life as an adventurer.

00:19.260 --> 00:20.630
Lorraine...

00:21.400 --> 00:24.250
But that's not what you want, right?

00:25.080 --> 00:28.930
Even if you don't have the talent, 
even if it takes you years...

00:28.930 --> 00:31.570
You want to become one 
no matter what, right?

00:32.560 --> 00:34.600
A Mythril-class adventurer...

00:38.430 --> 00:40.970
Don't pretend you haven't 
already made your decision.

00:40.970 --> 00:43.360
This has been your dream 
for years, hasn't it?

00:44.690 --> 00:46.030
Yes.

00:46.030 --> 00:47.950
Ever since I was a child.

00:50.630 --> 00:51.760
What's wrong?

00:51.760 --> 00:53.930
No, don't worry about it.

00:53.930 --> 00:57.270
I just remembered something Sheila asked me.

00:57.270 --> 00:58.930
What did she ask you?

00:59.390 --> 01:00.790
Don't worry about it.

01:00.790 --> 01:04.030
Now that you've said that, I'm worried.

01:04.790 --> 01:06.640
Really worried.

01:09.990 --> 01:11.700
Fine, I'll tell you.

01:11.700 --> 01:14.970
I'll tell you, but if you don't 
want to answer, you don't have to.

01:15.940 --> 01:18.970
You know everything about 
me there is to know, don't you?

01:18.970 --> 01:19.730
I don't.

01:19.730 --> 01:21.350
There's a ton I don't know.

01:25.670 --> 01:32.020
Rentt, why did you decide to become 
a Mythril-class adventurer?

03:04.870 --> 03:09.000
<b>Rentt
Faina</b>

03:09.140 --> 03:11.100
I never told you?

03:13.640 --> 03:18.370
I've known you for long enough that 
I kind of expected that answer...

03:18.920 --> 03:20.050
Whatever.

03:20.510 --> 03:22.880
Just drink the blood of 
a vampire, or a troll,

03:22.880 --> 03:25.130
or whatever you want, and evolve already!

03:25.790 --> 03:28.000
That's kind of mean, isn't it?

03:28.000 --> 03:31.480
"It's wrong to ask an adventurer 
about their identity or past."

03:32.130 --> 03:34.930
"That's the unspoken rule of this job."

03:35.420 --> 03:38.190
You're the one who told me 
that all those years ago.

03:38.190 --> 03:42.070
Of course, I can't imagine you having 
any kind of dark secret in your past.

03:42.070 --> 03:45.570
But after you told me that, 
I couldn't exactly ask you.

03:46.120 --> 03:49.780
It just never came up, really...

03:50.820 --> 03:53.660
It's not that interesting a story, anyway.

03:58.430 --> 03:59.630
Revenge...

04:00.920 --> 04:03.100
No, that's not quite right.

04:03.450 --> 04:10.400
I wanted to become a person who could 
stop a tragedy from ever happening.

04:11.440 --> 04:12.570
Rentt.

04:13.220 --> 04:15.770
The village where I was 
born, Hathala Village,

04:15.770 --> 04:18.950
was nestled deep in the mountains 
far away from any city.

04:19.460 --> 04:23.810
My dad did the shopping for the whole village, 
and anything else that required going outside.

04:23.810 --> 04:28.820
I was five the first time my 
parents took me outside.

04:32.460 --> 04:33.610
Hey, Rentt.

04:34.260 --> 04:35.840
What, Jinlin?

04:35.840 --> 04:38.070
What do you think the town's like?

04:38.070 --> 04:41.170
I'm sure there's lots of 
stuff we've never seen!

04:41.170 --> 04:42.580
I can't wait!

04:44.240 --> 04:46.940
There's a lot of people, right?

04:46.940 --> 04:49.850
I'm scared of bandits and stuff.

04:49.850 --> 04:51.970
You're such a wimp, Rentt.

04:51.970 --> 04:53.130
If you're...

04:54.960 --> 04:58.360
If you're that wimpy you'll never 
be able to become an adventurer.

04:58.940 --> 05:00.260
Adventurer?

05:00.260 --> 05:00.980
Shh!

05:01.490 --> 05:03.660
Don't let your parents hear!

05:03.660 --> 05:04.990
Okay...

05:05.940 --> 05:09.480
I want to travel the world when I grow up!

05:09.820 --> 05:12.100
Waterfalls falling from islands 
floating in the sky...

05:12.100 --> 05:13.870
Towns surrounded by water...

05:13.870 --> 05:16.700
Castles that disappear like a mirage...

05:16.700 --> 05:19.320
There's a lot of amazing places, they say.

05:19.320 --> 05:21.700
But it sounds dangerous.

05:21.700 --> 05:25.790
Don't worry! I'll get 
strong and protect you!

05:27.760 --> 05:30.530
I was really shy back then.

05:31.270 --> 05:32.920
That's a surprise.

05:32.920 --> 05:36.650
I'd envisioned you swinging a wooden 
sword and practicing every day.

05:36.650 --> 05:38.890
That would’ve been Jinlin.

05:39.670 --> 05:42.190
She dragged me all around the town.

05:42.190 --> 05:44.350
We got one heck of a scolding 
from Granny later.

05:45.530 --> 05:48.960
But looking back, it was fun.

05:52.010 --> 05:54.630
We were attacked on the way back.

05:56.020 --> 05:57.070
By him.

05:59.710 --> 06:00.920
Granny!

06:01.970 --> 06:06.120
Get away from here, now...

06:06.430 --> 06:09.270
Granny! Granny!

06:22.790 --> 06:23.690
Rentt!

06:29.360 --> 06:32.200
Maybe it was an awful thing 
to do, leaving them behind.

06:33.210 --> 06:35.930
But we were sure...

06:35.930 --> 06:38.710
...that we were the only survivors.

06:52.260 --> 06:54.740
It has to have given up by now.

06:54.740 --> 06:55.620
Yeah.

07:15.960 --> 07:17.860
It's a horrible thought, looking back.

07:17.860 --> 07:21.890
The wolf monster was toying with us.

07:36.080 --> 07:37.690
Jinlin! Why?

07:40.420 --> 07:43.730
'cause I promised... I'd protect you.

07:45.460 --> 07:50.690
Get stronger, Rentt.

08:07.880 --> 08:09.290
Get back.

08:09.730 --> 08:11.690
I'll handle him.

08:40.860 --> 08:42.400
You still want a fight?

08:58.110 --> 08:59.290
You okay?

09:00.520 --> 09:01.500
Why...

09:04.110 --> 09:06.840
Why didn't you come sooner?

09:07.870 --> 09:10.720
I'm sorry. This is my fault.

09:11.140 --> 09:13.730
If I'd only gotten here sooner...

09:20.840 --> 09:23.220
After he drove the wolf off,

09:23.220 --> 09:28.370
the adventurer carried everyone's 
bodies back to the village.

09:34.190 --> 09:36.780
Oh, there you are.

09:37.510 --> 09:38.360
Hey...

09:41.250 --> 09:43.680
How can I become an adventurer?

09:44.710 --> 09:46.060
Why?

09:46.550 --> 09:49.450
My friend wanted to become one.

09:50.180 --> 09:51.200
So...

09:52.640 --> 09:53.630
I see.

09:55.860 --> 09:58.130
Rentt, how old are you?

09:58.930 --> 10:00.490
Five...

10:00.790 --> 10:05.400
I'm sorry, but you need to be 15 to 
register with the Adventurers Guild.

10:08.760 --> 10:12.120
So train hard in this village 
for the next ten years.

10:13.610 --> 10:16.730
First, you need to learn to fight well enough to battle a monster.

10:17.480 --> 10:19.200
And knowledge, you'll need that, too!

10:19.200 --> 10:21.900
Learn to read, write, and do arithmetic.

10:22.460 --> 10:27.070
Herbs, magic, and how to survive 
when you're in the wild.

10:27.590 --> 10:31.010
There must be hunters and old 
herbalists in this village.

10:31.010 --> 10:34.640
First, start by persuading 
them to teach you.

10:35.300 --> 10:36.910
I was surprised.

10:36.910 --> 10:41.400
Most grown-ups would just say, "Good luck!"

10:41.400 --> 10:43.510
But not him.

10:44.490 --> 10:48.050
And if I do all that, can 
I be a strong adventurer?

10:48.540 --> 10:50.260
I can't promise that.

10:50.570 --> 10:54.820
Knowledge and combat skill will 
only get you to the starting line.

10:55.340 --> 10:57.840
After that, it's up to how 
much effort you put in.

10:59.660 --> 11:00.670
Effort...

11:01.160 --> 11:03.570
Remember one more thing.

11:04.960 --> 11:07.310
My name is Wilfried Ryukker.

11:07.310 --> 11:09.310
A Mythril-class adventurer.

11:10.610 --> 11:12.070
Mythril...

11:13.520 --> 11:15.810
When you become an adventurer, come see me.

11:15.810 --> 11:19.020
I don't know where I'll be 
in a decade, of course...

11:19.580 --> 11:22.670
But as long as I'm alive, I'll 
probably be an adventurer.

11:26.060 --> 11:30.060
Listen. Don't die until you 
make your dream come true.

11:30.060 --> 11:30.920
I won't!

11:33.830 --> 11:36.160
So that's why.

11:36.160 --> 11:39.410
It happens a lot, way 
out in the countryside.

11:39.410 --> 11:42.570
So the "certain person" you 
mentioned long ago, was...

11:42.570 --> 11:45.130
Yes, that adventurer.

11:45.800 --> 11:48.780
I don't know if you have 
good luck or bad luck.

11:48.780 --> 11:51.550
The odds of randomly being saved 
by a Mythril-class adventurer

11:51.550 --> 11:54.020
are about the same as the odds 
of encountering a dragon.

11:54.780 --> 11:56.510
You've got that right.

11:56.510 --> 12:01.080
So you learned your kindness from him, huh?

12:01.080 --> 12:06.690
I'm sure he was a nice guy, 
but he must've understood...

12:07.520 --> 12:08.590
Understood what?

12:09.090 --> 12:14.430
Without a goal, I wasn't going 
to get back my will to live.

12:14.430 --> 12:15.820
I see.

12:15.820 --> 12:20.660
So that's why he made his advice 
as specific as he could, huh?

12:20.960 --> 12:22.170
I assume so.

12:23.230 --> 12:28.060
Someday I'll defeat the monster 
that killed my parents and Jinlin.

12:28.890 --> 12:32.700
After I become a Mythril-class 
adventurer, like Wilfried.

12:33.450 --> 12:36.740
A decade in the village, a decade in Maalt.

12:36.740 --> 12:38.720
You've spent 20 years at this, huh?

12:38.720 --> 12:40.890
And never got above Bronze, though.

12:43.820 --> 12:45.240
I'm scared to die.

12:45.740 --> 12:46.630
But...

12:47.390 --> 12:50.410
If you give up, you're as good as dead.

12:51.010 --> 12:54.210
I knew you were only 
pretending to be uncertain.

12:54.210 --> 12:57.060
Well, that's who you are.

12:57.060 --> 13:00.710
Don't worry. I'll give your 
bones a proper burial.

13:00.710 --> 13:03.610
That's about all I can do for you.

13:03.610 --> 13:04.660
I'm sorry.

13:05.070 --> 13:09.030
If something happens to me and 
I lose control, burn me to ash.

13:10.790 --> 13:13.310
I'm praying that won't happen.

13:37.650 --> 13:38.620
Rentt...

13:39.100 --> 13:41.680
I'm fine, at least for now.

13:43.760 --> 13:46.330
Looks like the blood was fake...

13:46.900 --> 13:48.980
Hey, Rentt! What's wrong?

13:53.930 --> 13:55.640
Keep control of yourself, Rentt!

14:00.300 --> 14:01.470
Rentt!

14:15.110 --> 14:16.750
<i>What is this sensation?</i>

14:17.350 --> 14:21.170
<i>It's like my body is being remade...</i>

14:22.340 --> 14:24.580
<i>I... I...</i>

14:25.020 --> 14:28.010
<i>I don't want to become 
one of those monsters!</i>

14:28.010 --> 14:29.270
<i>I...</i>

14:29.270 --> 14:30.140
Rentt.

14:30.540 --> 14:31.510
Rentt.

14:33.830 --> 14:38.020
You have a dream... a goal, dont you?

14:41.880 --> 14:42.940
So...

14:44.310 --> 14:45.550
Come back.

15:11.440 --> 15:15.580
It's not gonna be worth a damn 
without orichalcum, huh?

15:18.010 --> 15:22.100
You don't have to start this early, darling.

15:23.350 --> 15:25.800
Oh, it's for him, isn't it?

15:25.800 --> 15:29.250
But didn't you just give him a sword?

15:34.420 --> 15:38.240
I can't tell, but he's gotten 
a lot stronger, hasn't he?

15:39.640 --> 15:40.820
Yeah.

15:40.820 --> 15:43.450
He's even picked up some weird tricks.

15:43.780 --> 15:46.870
Then we need to make 
him a worthy sword.

15:49.800 --> 15:51.220
I have been defeated!

15:51.220 --> 15:53.620
Hey, let me be an adventurer, next!

15:53.620 --> 15:55.230
I'll be the wizard, then!

15:55.230 --> 15:57.620
What? I'm the monster again?

16:03.130 --> 16:06.120
Oh my. Such a brave knight.

16:06.670 --> 16:08.910
Or an adventurer, perhaps?

16:08.910 --> 16:12.490
You need to be in bed, Headmistress Lilian!

16:12.490 --> 16:14.010
I'm fine.

16:14.010 --> 16:16.030
I feel wonderful today.

16:16.500 --> 16:20.110
May I eat with you all today?

16:20.750 --> 16:22.110
Of course.

16:22.110 --> 16:23.540
Everyone will be overjoyed.

16:24.840 --> 16:26.850
Thank you, Alize.

16:27.950 --> 16:32.510
It's thanks to you that 
I'm doing better now.

16:33.550 --> 16:35.980
That's not true, Headmistress Lilian.

16:36.420 --> 16:40.500
Everyone... everyone helped!

16:43.360 --> 16:46.090
Morning!

16:46.090 --> 16:48.350
Okay, I'm first here again today!

16:48.350 --> 16:50.260
Ryze!

16:51.450 --> 16:53.610
Wait up!

16:53.610 --> 16:55.790
Are you okay, Laura?

16:55.790 --> 16:57.510
Good morning.

16:58.110 --> 17:00.070
Good morning!

17:00.070 --> 17:03.000
We have a whole bunch of new jobs today!

17:04.050 --> 17:06.260
It was worth coming early!

17:06.260 --> 17:08.470
Yeah! Let's go, Rina!

17:09.150 --> 17:12.180
Anything good, Ryze?

17:12.180 --> 17:15.640
I still can't read some of these 
letters, but how about this one?

17:15.640 --> 17:17.120
The pay's good.

17:17.120 --> 17:20.200
No way! It says it's the second floor.

17:20.200 --> 17:24.240
That's right. Only take jobs that 
are a good fit for your strength.

17:24.240 --> 17:26.110
How about this one?

17:26.110 --> 17:29.310
Hmm... seems good to me!

17:29.310 --> 17:29.700
Right?

17:29.700 --> 17:33.080
Everyone, be careful if you're 
going to the labyrinth.

17:33.770 --> 17:37.730
It's important to turn back if 
even the slightest thing feels off.

17:37.730 --> 17:39.630
Yes, we'll remember that.

17:39.630 --> 17:41.850
An adventurer must never 
let their guard down!

17:41.850 --> 17:42.790
Right!

17:42.790 --> 17:46.550
And... you only get one shot at life!

17:55.490 --> 17:57.780
I want a little more sleep...

17:59.840 --> 18:04.260
It's been so long since I've felt sleepy...

18:06.150 --> 18:08.220
<i>Ever since I became an undead,</i>

18:08.220 --> 18:11.130
<i>it was like my whole body was 
empty, down to my heart.</i>

18:12.110 --> 18:18.170
<i>But with each evolution,
I gained organs... skin...</i>

18:18.900 --> 18:21.400
<i>That horrible feeling... the pain...</i>

18:22.520 --> 18:27.250
<i>The fear and despair at becoming 
something that wasn't me...</i>

18:30.550 --> 18:35.090
I guess I only endured it 
because I was immortal, huh?

18:45.420 --> 18:47.430
What are you reading?

18:48.100 --> 18:49.730
You're awake?

18:50.290 --> 18:51.210
Yeah...

18:51.210 --> 18:55.130
I was reading a book about vampire ecology.

18:55.830 --> 19:00.000
Ghast. Lesser vampire. Middle. Greater.

19:00.440 --> 19:04.470
The more powerful they become, 
the rarer it is to see one.

19:04.470 --> 19:06.140
And the harder it becomes to classify them.

19:08.090 --> 19:09.870
Why are you reading that?

19:09.870 --> 19:11.720
That's an easy question to answer.

19:11.720 --> 19:12.760
Basically...

19:13.340 --> 19:16.000
Congratulations on your evolution.

19:22.750 --> 19:25.170
What did I become?

19:25.450 --> 19:27.190
I'll check for you.

19:27.190 --> 19:28.700
Start by taking off your clothes.

19:34.270 --> 19:36.180
What are these?

19:36.860 --> 19:38.000
Wings?

19:41.650 --> 19:44.280
You can shrink them by 
focusing on them, huh?

19:44.280 --> 19:45.570
That's good for you.

19:45.570 --> 19:47.300
It sure is.

19:47.300 --> 19:49.990
I never would've been able 
to go out in public again.

19:50.510 --> 19:53.550
Hey, so what did I become?

19:53.550 --> 19:54.700
I don't know.

19:54.700 --> 19:58.310
But whatever it is, it's 
a more powerful being.

19:58.310 --> 20:01.070
I assume it's one of the 
weaker types of vampires,

20:01.070 --> 20:03.520
but I've never heard of one with wings.

20:03.520 --> 20:04.670
I see.

20:04.970 --> 20:07.450
I'll look into the wings later.

20:07.450 --> 20:09.160
Start by showing me your face.

20:09.160 --> 20:10.300
Okay.

20:11.660 --> 20:12.780
Open your mouth.

20:14.760 --> 20:17.120
I see small fangs...

20:17.120 --> 20:19.910
You're very likely a vampire, then.

20:19.910 --> 20:21.100
Now the top.

20:21.100 --> 20:22.000
Okay.

20:28.580 --> 20:29.450
Well?

20:29.880 --> 20:31.980
Your eyes are red.

20:32.580 --> 20:34.880
That's something vampires
are well known for,

20:34.880 --> 20:37.440
but there are also humans with red eyes.

20:37.440 --> 20:40.190
On its own, that's not enough 
for you to be found out.

20:42.290 --> 20:43.530
More importantly...

20:45.940 --> 20:48.380
It feels like a face I haven't 
seen in a long time.

20:49.200 --> 20:52.950
I know it's late, but there's something 
I want to say to that face.

20:53.420 --> 20:54.350
What?

20:54.710 --> 20:56.280
What else?

21:00.650 --> 21:03.480
Welcome home, Rentt Faina.

21:07.510 --> 21:08.360
Thanks.

21:09.290 --> 21:10.390
I'm home.

22:35.530 --> 22:37.670
Sorry to drag you out here with me.

22:37.670 --> 22:40.900
It's fine. It's my thanks for 
everything you've done for me.

22:41.560 --> 22:44.920
Hey, did you ever go see Wilfried?

22:45.370 --> 22:49.640
I looked for him a bunch, but he's 
not in this country, I think.

22:49.960 --> 22:52.380
Another country, then.

22:52.380 --> 22:56.140
But it's dangerous for a Bronze-class 
to go on long journeys alone, right?

22:56.140 --> 22:57.270
True.

22:57.800 --> 23:03.850
And part of me didn't want to go until 
I felt a bit more worthy, actually.

23:04.640 --> 23:08.770
And that's why you haven't 
gone to see him for 20 years.

23:08.770 --> 23:10.550
Yeah, that's right.

23:11.660 --> 23:12.890
Thanks.

23:14.670 --> 23:17.040
But right now, I could go.

23:18.270 --> 23:19.730
I could go see him.

23:25.410 --> 23:27.110
Do what you want.

23:27.960 --> 23:30.390
You don't listen to a word I say, after all.

23:30.390 --> 23:33.100
You'll get a chance sometime, I'm sure.

23:33.100 --> 23:34.220
Yeah.

23:34.220 --> 23:36.620
I wouldn't mind coming along
if I'm not doing anything.

23:36.620 --> 23:38.610
Glad to hear it.
